<%# Path 2 — Turbo-Stream-appended toasts. The container below is rendered once (in
    a real app: once, in the layout, outside any frame — data-turbo-permanent keeps
    it and its contents untouched across a page morph). A later controller response
    only ever appends into it; the whole server-side story is one line:
      def create
        @order.save!
        render turbo_stream: turbo_stream.append(
          Crosswire::UI::ToastViewport::DEFAULT_ID) { cw.toast("Order placed.", severity: :success) }
      end
    This example renders the container plus what that append would add, standing in
    for the Turbo Stream round trip a static gallery page cannot itself perform. %>
<%= cw.toast_viewport %>
<%= turbo_stream.append Crosswire::UI::ToastViewport::DEFAULT_ID do %>
  <%= cw.toast "Order placed.", severity: :success %>
<% end %>
